# Scroll Anchoring

The browser's native scroll anchoring automatically adjusts `scrollTop` when content above the viewport changes height. In dynamic UIs (chat, citation panels, lazy-loaded embeds), this causes the page to jump unexpectedly when content is added, removed, or resizes.

**Fix:** disable scroll anchoring on the scrollable container and its inner content wrapper.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — stable scroll position when child content changes height
<main
  className="flex-1 overflow-y-auto"
  style={{ overflowAnchor: "none" }}
>
  <div style={{ overflowAnchor: "none" }}>
    {/* dynamic content: panels, embeds, images */}
  </div>
</main>

// ❌ BAD — scroll jumps when citation panel opens/closes or embed images load
<main className="flex-1 overflow-y-auto">
  <div>
    {/* dynamic content */}
  </div>
</main>
```

Apply `overflowAnchor: "none"` to both the scroll container **and** the direct inner wrapper — browsers can re-enable anchoring on children by default.
